/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Ezra chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("ezra", [
{n:1, name:"Cyrus's Decree", seal:{ref:"Ezra 1:3",verse:"Who is there among you of all his people? his God be with him, and let him go up to Jerusalem, which is in Judah, and build the house of the LORD God of Israel, (he is the God,) which is in Jerusalem."}, facts:["Did you know? Cyrus's decree fulfilled a prophecy. Jeremiah had foretold the return from exile, and the LORD stirred a Persian king's heart to make it happen.","Did you know? The vessels Nebuchadnezzar stole were counted one by one. Thirty chargers of gold, a thousand of silver, and more, 5,400 pieces in all, handed back to Sheshbazzar.","Did you know? Cyrus invited anyone to go, but only those whose spirit God raised actually rose up. The call was wide, and the response was personal."], questions:[
{q:"In whose first year did the LORD stir up the king's spirit to fulfill Jeremiah's word?", options:["Cyrus king of Persia","Darius king of Persia","Artaxerxes king of Persia","Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:1",verse:"Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the word of the LORD by the mouth of Jeremiah might be fulfilled, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying,", insight:"God keeps His promises right on schedule, and He can move even a foreign king's heart to do it."},
{q:"According to Cyrus's decree, what had the LORD charged him to do?", options:["Build him an house at Jerusalem","Carry the vessels to Babylon","Number the returning exiles","Rebuild the walls of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:2",verse:"Thus saith Cyrus king of Persia, The LORD God of heaven hath given me all the kingdoms of the earth; and he hath charged me to build him an house at Jerusalem, which is in Judah.", insight:"Cyrus knew his power came from God. Every gift and position we hold is a trust to use for His purposes."},
{q:"Cyrus asked, 'Who is there among you of all his people?' Where did he say they should go up to?", options:["Jerusalem, which is in Judah","Babylon, which is in Chaldea","Shushan, which is in Elam","Samaria, which is in Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:3",verse:"Who is there among you of all his people? his God be with him, and let him go up to Jerusalem, which is in Judah, and build the house of the LORD God of Israel, (he is the God,) which is in Jerusalem.", insight:"The invitation was open to all God's people. God still calls each of us by name to take part in His work."},
{q:"Those who remained in any place were told to help with silver, gold, goods, and beasts, plus what?", options:["The freewill offering for the house of God","The yearly tax to the king","Provisions for the king's army","Oil for the lamps of the temple"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:4",verse:"And whosoever remaineth in any place where he sojourneth, let the men of his place help him with silver, and with gold, and with goods, and with beasts, beside the freewill offering for the house of God that is in Jerusalem.", insight:"Those who stayed behind could still share in the work by giving. You do not have to go to be part of what God is doing."},
{q:"Which groups rose up, led by the chief of the fathers of Judah and Benjamin, to build the house?", options:["The priests, and the Levites, with all them whose spirit God had raised","The singers and the porters only","The treasurers and the guards","The governors of the provinces"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:5",verse:"Then rose up the chief of the fathers of Judah and Benjamin, and the priests, and the Levites, with all them whose spirit God had raised, to go up to build the house of the LORD which is in Jerusalem.", insight:"Only those whose spirit God raised rose up. Real movement toward God begins in the heart, not in the crowd."},
{q:"Their neighbors strengthened their hands with vessels of silver, gold, goods, beasts, and what else?", options:["Precious things","Swords and shields","Cedar timber","Purple garments"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:6",verse:"And all they that were about them strengthened their hands with vessels of silver, with gold, with goods, and with beasts, and with precious things, beside all that was willingly offered.", insight:"Neighbors strengthened the builders' hands with generous gifts. God often provides through the people around us."},
{q:"What did Cyrus bring forth that Nebuchadnezzar had taken out of Jerusalem?", options:["The vessels of the house of the LORD","The stones of the city walls","The crowns of the kings of Judah","The scrolls of the law"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:7",verse:"Also Cyrus the king brought forth the vessels of the house of the LORD, which Nebuchadnezzar had brought forth out of Jerusalem, and had put them in the house of his gods;", insight:"What was stolen in judgment was restored in mercy. God does not forget what belongs to His house."},
{q:"By whose hand did Cyrus bring forth the vessels?", options:["Mithredath the treasurer","Sheshbazzar the prince","Tatnai the governor","Shetharboznai the scribe"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:8",verse:"Even those did Cyrus king of Persia bring forth by the hand of Mithredath the treasurer, and numbered them unto Sheshbazzar, the prince of Judah.", insight:"God used a Persian treasurer to handle holy things. He can use unlikely people in positions of trust."},
{q:"To whom were the vessels numbered, the prince of Judah?", options:["Sheshbazzar","Zerubbabel","Jeshua","Nehemiah"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:8",verse:"Even those did Cyrus king of Persia bring forth by the hand of Mithredath the treasurer, and numbered them unto Sheshbazzar, the prince of Judah.", insight:"The vessels were numbered and handed to a named leader. God cares about order and accountability in His work."},
{q:"How many chargers of gold were among the vessels?", options:["Thirty","A thousand","Nine and twenty","Four hundred and ten"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:9",verse:"And this is the number of them: thirty chargers of gold, a thousand chargers of silver, nine and twenty knives,", insight:"Even the small items were counted: thirty chargers of gold. Nothing given to God is too small to be recorded."},
{q:"How many chargers of silver were numbered?", options:["A thousand","Thirty","Four hundred and ten","Five thousand and four hundred"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:9",verse:"And this is the number of them: thirty chargers of gold, a thousand chargers of silver, nine and twenty knives,", insight:"A thousand chargers of silver shows the scale of restoration. God returns more than we expect."},
{q:"How many basons of gold were numbered among the vessels?", options:["Thirty","A thousand","Nine and twenty","Four hundred and ten"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:10",verse:"Thirty basons of gold, silver basons of a second sort four hundred and ten, and other vessels a thousand.", insight:"Thirty basons of gold, each counted. God keeps careful account of what is given to Him."},
{q:"What was the total of all the vessels of gold and of silver?", options:["Five thousand and four hundred","Two thousand and five hundred","A thousand and three hundred","Forty and two thousand three hundred"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:11",verse:"All the vessels of gold and of silver were five thousand and four hundred. All these did Sheshbazzar bring up with them of the captivity that were brought up from Babylon unto Jerusalem.", insight:"All 5,400 pieces came home. When God restores, He restores completely."},
{q:"Sheshbazzar brought up the vessels with whom?", options:["Them of the captivity that were brought up from Babylon unto Jerusalem","The army of Cyrus from Persia","The masons of Tyre and Sidon","The priests of the captivity in Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:11",verse:"All the vessels of gold and of silver were five thousand and four hundred. All these did Sheshbazzar bring up with them of the captivity that were brought up from Babylon unto Jerusalem.", insight:"Sheshbazzar carried the vessels up from Babylon to Jerusalem. God raises leaders to carry His work forward."},
{q:"Why did the LORD stir up the spirit of Cyrus in the first place?", options:["That the word of the LORD by the mouth of Jeremiah might be fulfilled","To punish the remnant of Judah","To enrich the treasury of Persia","To settle the disputes of the nations"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:1",verse:"Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the word of the LORD by the mouth of Jeremiah might be fulfilled, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying,", insight:"The whole return hinged on Jeremiah's fulfilled word. God's promises never expire."},
{q:"Who was to help the one who remained behind in any place?", options:["The men of his place","The priests of Jerusalem","The treasurer of Persia","The governor of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:4",verse:"And whosoever remaineth in any place where he sojourneth, let the men of his place help him with silver, and with gold, and with goods, and with beasts, beside the freewill offering for the house of God that is in Jerusalem.", insight:"The men of his place were to help. God asks those nearest to us to share in the work."},
{q:"Cyrus said the LORD God of heaven had given him what?", options:["All the kingdoms of the earth","The treasures of Babylon","A mighty army","Seventy years of peace"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:2",verse:"Thus saith Cyrus king of Persia, The LORD God of heaven hath given me all the kingdoms of the earth; and he hath charged me to build him an house at Jerusalem, which is in Judah.", insight:"Cyrus confessed that God gave him all kingdoms. True greatness admits where its power comes from."},
{q:"Who rose up to go to Jerusalem when Cyrus made his decree?", options:["The chief of the fathers of Judah and Benjamin, the priests, and the Levites","Only the tribe of Judah","The Persian governors","The Nethinims alone"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:5",verse:"Then rose up the chief of the fathers of Judah and Benjamin, and the priests, and the Levites, with all them whose spirit God had raised, to go up to build the house of the LORD which is in Jerusalem.", insight:"God stirred their spirits and they rose. When God moves, His people get up and go."},
{q:"How many silver basons of a second sort were numbered?", options:["Four hundred and ten","Thirty","Nine and twenty","A thousand"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:10",verse:"Thirty basons of gold, silver basons of a second sort four hundred and ten, and other vessels a thousand.", insight:"Four hundred and ten silver basons, each counted. Faithfulness includes careful stewardship of details."},
{q:"What had Nebuchadnezzar done with the vessels he took from Jerusalem?", options:["Put them in the house of his gods","Broken them in pieces","Sold them for silver","Cast them into the river"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 1:7",verse:"Also Cyrus the king brought forth the vessels of the house of the LORD, which Nebuchadnezzar had brought forth out of Jerusalem, and had put them in the house of his gods;", insight:"Nebuchadnezzar had put God's vessels in the house of his gods. What sin misuses, God reclaims for holy use."}
]},
{n:2, name:"The Returning Exiles", seal:{ref:"Ezra 2:64",verse:"The whole congregation together was forty and two thousand three hundred and threescore,"}, facts:["Did you know? The returning company was counted at 42,360 people. Ezra 2 holds one of the longest name lists in the Bible, family by family.","Did you know? Some priests were barred from serving because their family records were missing. Without proof of lineage, they could not eat the most holy things until a priest with Urim and Thummim decided.","Did you know? The exiles brought 736 horses, 245 mules, 435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys. The caravan back to Judah was enormous."], questions:[
{q:"What were the children of the province doing at the start of the chapter?", options:["Going up out of the captivity, returning every one unto his city","Fleeing from Babylon to Egypt","Gathering in Babylon to build a temple","Returning to Persia for the feast"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:1",verse:"Now these are the children of the province that went up out of the captivity, of those which had been carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away unto Babylon, and came again unto Jerusalem and Judah, every one unto his city;", insight:"Each exile returned every one unto his city. God restores people to their own place and calling."},
{q:"Which man is named alongside Zerubbabel in verse 2?", options:["Jeshua","Haggai","Sheshbazzar","Daniel"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:2",verse:"Which came with Zerubbabel: Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mizpar, Bigvai, Rehum, Baanah. The number of the men of the people of Israel:", insight:"Jeshua stood beside Zerubbabel from the start. God's work moves forward through faithful partnerships."},
{q:"How many were the children of Parosh?", options:["Two thousand an hundred seventy and two","Two thousand and twelve","A thousand two hundred fifty and four","Nine hundred forty and five"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:3",verse:"The children of Parosh, two thousand an hundred seventy and two.", insight:"Parosh's family numbered 2,172, the largest listed. God knows and counts every family that answers His call."},
{q:"How many were the children of Elam?", options:["A thousand two hundred fifty and four","Two thousand an hundred seventy and two","Nine hundred forty and five","Six hundred sixty and six"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:7",verse:"The children of Elam, a thousand two hundred fifty and four.", insight:"Elam's 1,254 show that whole clans moved together. Faith often travels in families."},
{q:"Which family numbered six hundred sixty and six?", options:["Adonikam","Bigvai","Adin","Ater"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:13",verse:"The children of Adonikam, six hundred sixty and six.", insight:"Even a family of 666 was recorded by name. In God's book, no family is too small or too ordinary to be listed."},
{q:"How many priests, the children of Jedaiah, of the house of Jeshua, returned?", options:["Nine hundred seventy and three","A thousand fifty and two","A thousand two hundred forty and seven","A thousand and seventeen"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:36",verse:"The priests: the children of Jedaiah, of the house of Jeshua, nine hundred seventy and three.", insight:"Nine hundred seventy three priests of Jedaiah's line returned. God preserved a worshiping priesthood through exile."},
{q:"How many Levites, the children of Jeshua and Kadmiel, came up?", options:["Seventy and four","An hundred twenty and eight","An hundred thirty and nine","Two hundred"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:40",verse:"The Levites: the children of Jeshua and Kadmiel, of the children of Hodaviah, seventy and four.", insight:"Only seventy four Levites came, far fewer than the priests. God can do much with few when hearts are willing."},
{q:"The singers, the children of Asaph, numbered what?", options:["An hundred twenty and eight","Seventy and four","An hundred thirty and nine","Two hundred"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:41",verse:"The singers: the children of Asaph, an hundred twenty and eight.", insight:"The sons of Asaph, 128 singers, came to lead worship. Music and praise were essential to the restored community, not decoration."},
{q:"How many porters returned?", options:["An hundred thirty and nine","An hundred twenty and eight","Seventy and four","Four hundred fifty and four"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:42",verse:"The children of the porters: the children of Shallum, the children of Ater, the children of Talmon, the children of Akkub, the children of Hatita, the children of Shobai, in all an hundred thirty and nine.", insight:"One hundred thirty nine porters guarded the house. Every role matters, including the quiet work of keeping watch."},
{q:"What was the number of the whole congregation together?", options:["Forty and two thousand three hundred and threescore","Sixty thousand","Twenty and nine thousand","Seventy thousand"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:64",verse:"The whole congregation together was forty and two thousand three hundred and threescore,", insight:"The total, 42,360, shows a remnant, not the whole nation. God often works through a faithful few."},
{q:"Besides the congregation, how many singing men and singing women were there?", options:["Two hundred","Seven hundred thirty and six","Four hundred thirty and five","Six thousand seven hundred and twenty"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:65",verse:"Beside their servants and their maids, of whom there were seven thousand three hundred thirty and seven: and there were among them two hundred singing men and singing women.", insight:"Two hundred singers among the servants show that worship belonged to all classes, not just leaders."},
{q:"How many horses did the returning company have?", options:["Seven hundred thirty and six","Two hundred forty and five","Four hundred thirty and five","Six thousand seven hundred and twenty"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:66",verse:"Their horses were seven hundred thirty and six; their mules, two hundred forty and five;", insight:"Seven hundred thirty six horses speak of a long, hard journey. Following God costs something real."},
{q:"How many camels did they have?", options:["Four hundred thirty and five","Seven hundred thirty and six","Two hundred forty and five","Six thousand seven hundred and twenty"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:67",verse:"Their camels, four hundred thirty and five; their asses, six thousand seven hundred and twenty.", insight:"Four hundred thirty five camels carried the load. God provides the means for the journey He commands."},
{q:"How many asses were in the caravan?", options:["Six thousand seven hundred and twenty","Seven hundred thirty and six","Two hundred forty and five","Four hundred thirty and five"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:67",verse:"Their camels, four hundred thirty and five; their asses, six thousand seven hundred and twenty.", insight:"Six thousand seven hundred twenty donkeys, the workhorses of the caravan. Ordinary strength, given to God, moves His work."},
{q:"What did some of the chief of the fathers do when they came to the house of the LORD at Jerusalem?", options:["Offered freely for the house of God","Paid silver into the king's treasury","Brought a peace offering for the king","Presented the firstfruits of the harvest"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:68",verse:"And some of the chief of the fathers, when they came to the house of the LORD which is at Jerusalem, offered freely for the house of God to set it up in his place:", insight:"The fathers gave freely for God's house before it existed. Generosity of faith gives toward what is not yet seen."},
{q:"Why were some who sought their genealogy called polluted and put from the priesthood?", options:["They could not find their register among those reckoned by genealogy","They had married foreign wives","They had no offering to bring","They arrived a month too late"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:62",verse:"These sought their register among those that were reckoned by genealogy, but they were not found: therefore were they, as polluted, put from the priesthood.", insight:"Missing records kept men from the priesthood. God takes holiness and calling seriously; not everyone may do sacred work."},
{q:"The Tirshatha said they should not eat of the most holy things until what happened?", options:["There stood up a priest with Urim and with Thummim","The temple was finished","The king gave permission","The feast of tabernacles came"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:63",verse:"And the Tirshatha said unto them, that they should not eat of the most holy things, till there stood up a priest with Urim and with Thummim.", insight:"They waited for a priest with Urim and Thummim. Some questions are settled by waiting on God's appointed means."},
{q:"Where did the priests, Levites, singers, porters, and Nethinims dwell?", options:["In their cities","In Jerusalem only","In tents by the river","In Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:70",verse:"So the priests, and the Levites, and some of the people, and the singers, and the porters, and the Nethinims, dwelt in their cities, and all Israel in their cities.", insight:"Each group dwelt in their own cities. Restoration meant resettling real life, not just rebuilding walls."},
{q:"Whose name heads the list of those who came up in verse 2?", options:["Zerubbabel","Jeshua","Nehemiah","Seraiah"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:2",verse:"Which came with Zerubbabel: Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mizpar, Bigvai, Rehum, Baanah. The number of the men of the people of Israel:", insight:"Zerubbabel's name heads the list. God puts a leader's name first, but the whole list shows the people mattered."},
{q:"How many were the children of Bigvai?", options:["Two thousand fifty and six","Two thousand an hundred seventy and two","Nine hundred forty and five","Six hundred forty and two"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 2:14",verse:"The children of Bigvai, two thousand fifty and six.", insight:"Bigvai's 2,056 families joined the return. Large or small, every family that came was written down."}
]}
,
{n:3, name:"The Foundation Laid", seal:{ref:"Ezra 3:11",verse:"And they sang together by course in praising and giving thanks unto the LORD; because he is good, for his mercy endureth for ever toward Israel. And all the people shouted with a great shout, when they praised the LORD, because the foundation of the house of the LORD was laid."}, facts:["Did you know? The altar went up before the temple did. Sacrifices resumed on the first day of the seventh month, even while the foundation was still unlaid.","Did you know? The temple timber came by sea. Cedar from Lebanon was floated to Joppa under Cyrus's grant, just as in Solomon's day.","Did you know? The foundation ceremony mixed tears and cheers. Old men who had seen Solomon's temple wept, while the young shouted for joy, and no one could tell the sounds apart."], questions:[
{q:"In which month did the people gather as one man to Jerusalem?", options:["The seventh month","The first month","The second month","The twelfth month"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:1",verse:"And when the seventh month was come, and the children of Israel were in the cities, the people gathered themselves together as one man to Jerusalem.", insight:"The people gathered as one man. Unity was the first building material of the restored temple."},
{q:"Who, with Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, built the altar of the God of Israel?", options:["Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and his brethren the priests","Ezra the scribe","Nehemiah the governor","Mordecai the Benjamite"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:2",verse:"Then stood up Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and his brethren the priests, and Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and his brethren, and builded the altar of the God of Israel, to offer burnt offerings thereon, as it is written in the law of Moses the man of God.", insight:"Jeshua and Zerubbabel led together, priest and governor side by side. God's work needs both worship and leadership."},
{q:"Why did they build the altar first?", options:["To offer burnt offerings thereon","To store the temple treasures","To mark the city boundary","To shelter the workmen"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:2",verse:"Then stood up Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and his brethren the priests, and Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and his brethren, and builded the altar of the God of Israel, to offer burnt offerings thereon, as it is written in the law of Moses the man of God.", insight:"The altar came before the temple. Worship and sacrifice take priority over buildings."},
{q:"Why did they set the altar upon his bases even though fear was upon them?", options:["Because of the people of those countries","Because the king commanded haste","Because the rains were coming","Because the priests were few"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:3",verse:"And they set the altar upon his bases; for fear was upon them because of the people of those countries: and they offered burnt offerings thereon unto the LORD, even burnt offerings morning and evening.", insight:"They built though fear was upon them. Courage is obeying God while afraid, not waiting until fear leaves."},
{q:"Which feast did they keep, as it is written?", options:["The feast of tabernacles","The feast of unleavened bread","The feast of weeks","The feast of trumpets"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:4",verse:"They kept also the feast of tabernacles, as it is written, and offered the daily burnt offerings by number, according to the custom, as the duty of every day required;", insight:"They kept the feast as it is written. Restoration meant returning to God's Word, not inventing new ways."},
{q:"From which day did they begin to offer burnt offerings unto the LORD?", options:["The first day of the seventh month","The tenth day of the seventh month","The first day of the first month","The fourteenth day of the first month"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:6",verse:"From the first day of the seventh month began they to offer burnt offerings unto the LORD. But the foundation of the temple of the LORD was not yet laid.", insight:"Offerings began on the first day of the seventh month. They did not wait for perfect conditions to worship."},
{q:"What had not yet been laid when they began offering?", options:["The foundation of the temple of the LORD","The walls of the city","The gates of Jerusalem","The courts of the priests"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:6",verse:"From the first day of the seventh month began they to offer burnt offerings unto the LORD. But the foundation of the temple of the LORD was not yet laid.", insight:"The foundation was not yet laid, but worship had begun. You can honor God before the work is finished."},
{q:"What did they give to them of Sidon and of Tyre?", options:["Meat, and drink, and oil","Gold and silver vessels","Wheat and wine only","Timber from Bashan"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:7",verse:"They gave money also unto the masons, and to the carpenters; and meat, and drink, and oil, unto them of Zidon, and to them of Tyre, to bring cedar trees from Lebanon to the sea of Joppa, according to the grant that they had of Cyrus king of Persia.", insight:"Meat, drink, and oil went to Sidon and Tyre. God's work creates honest trade and friendship with neighbors."},
{q:"What did the men of Sidon and Tyre bring in return?", options:["Cedar trees from Lebanon to the sea of Joppa","Stones from the quarries of Moab","Iron from the mines of Tarshish","Linen from Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:7",verse:"They gave money also unto the masons, and to the carpenters; and meat, and drink, and oil, unto them of Zidon, and to them of Tyre, to bring cedar trees from Lebanon to the sea of Joppa, according to the grant that they had of Cyrus king of Persia.", insight:"Cedar floated from Lebanon to Joppa, as in Solomon's day. God was repeating His ancient pattern of provision."},
{q:"What did Zerubbabel and Jeshua appoint the Levites, from twenty years old and upward, to do?", options:["To set forward the work of the house of the LORD","To sing with cymbals at the gates","To keep the doors of the temple","To number the returning people"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:8",verse:"Now in the second year of their coming unto the house of God at Jerusalem, in the second month, began Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and the remnant of their brethren the priests and the Levites, and all they that were come out of the captivity unto Jerusalem; and appointed the Levites, from twenty years old and upward, to set forward the work of the house of the LORD.", insight:"The Levites from twenty years old and upward were set to the work. God enlists the young in serious service."},
{q:"In what year and month did they begin to set forward the work of the house?", options:["The second year of their coming, in the second month","The first year, in the seventh month","The seventh year, in the first month","The twentieth year, in the month Nisan"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:8",verse:"Now in the second year of their coming unto the house of God at Jerusalem, in the second month, began Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and the remnant of their brethren the priests and the Levites, and all they that were come out of the captivity unto Jerusalem; and appointed the Levites, from twenty years old and upward, to set forward the work of the house of the LORD.", insight:"The work began in the second year, second month. God's timing had a set start, and obedience met the schedule."},
{q:"Who stood to set forward the workmen of the house of God?", options:["Jeshua with his sons and his brethren, Kadmiel and his sons","The sons of Asaph with cymbals","The porters with their trumpets","The Nethinims with the timber"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:9",verse:"Then stood Jeshua with his sons and his brethren, Kadmiel and his sons, the sons of Judah, together, to set forward the workmen in the house of God: the sons of Henadad, with their sons and their brethren the Levites.", insight:"Jeshua, Kadmiel, and their sons set the workmen forward. Families serving together multiply strength."},
{q:"When the builders laid the foundation, how were the priests set?", options:["In their apparel with trumpets","In white linen with harps","With torches at the gates","With the ark on their shoulders"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:10",verse:"And when the builders laid the foundation of the temple of the LORD, they set the priests in their apparel with trumpets, and the Levites the sons of Asaph with cymbals, to praise the LORD, after the ordinance of David king of Israel.", insight:"Priests in apparel with trumpets marked the moment. Milestones in God's work deserve celebration."},
{q:"The Levites, the sons of Asaph, held what instruments?", options:["Cymbals","Trumpets","Harps","Psalteries"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:10",verse:"And when the builders laid the foundation of the temple of the LORD, they set the priests in their apparel with trumpets, and the Levites the sons of Asaph with cymbals, to praise the LORD, after the ordinance of David king of Israel.", insight:"The sons of Asaph with cymbals kept the music in Levite hands. Worship leadership is a sacred trust."},
{q:"Besides the continual burnt offering, what else did they offer?", options:["The offerings of the new moons and set feasts, and freewill offerings","Only the morning sacrifice","The sin offering for the king","The wave offering of the priests"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:5",verse:"And afterward offered the continual burnt offering, both of the new moons, and of all the set feasts of the LORD that were consecrated, and of every one that willingly offered a freewill offering unto the LORD.", insight:"New moons, set feasts, and freewill offerings all resumed. A restored people keep the full rhythm of worship."},
{q:"What words did they sing together by course?", options:["Because he is good, for his mercy endureth for ever toward Israel","Holy, holy, holy is the LORD of hosts","Blessed be the LORD God of Israel for ever","The LORD reigneth, let the earth rejoice"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:11",verse:"And they sang together by course in praising and giving thanks unto the LORD; because he is good, for his mercy endureth for ever toward Israel. And all the people shouted with a great shout, when they praised the LORD, because the foundation of the house of the LORD was laid.", insight:"His mercy endureth for ever toward Israel was their song. Gratitude for mercy is the church's oldest chorus."},
{q:"What did the old priests and Levites who had seen the first house do when the foundation was laid?", options:["Wept with a loud voice","Kept silent in grief","Refused to sing","Left the assembly"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:12",verse:"But many of the priests and Levites and chief of the fathers, who were ancient men, that had seen the first house, when the foundation of this house was laid before their eyes, wept with a loud voice; and many shouted aloud for joy:", insight:"They wept remembering the former glory, while others shouted for joy. God holds both tears and triumph in the same moment."},
{q:"Why did the ancient men who had seen the first house weep with a loud voice?", options:["They remembered the former house","They feared the work would fail","They grieved for their sins","They mourned the dead"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:12",verse:"But many of the priests and Levites and chief of the fathers, who were ancient men, that had seen the first house, when the foundation of this house was laid before their eyes, wept with a loud voice; and many shouted aloud for joy:", insight:"The old men wept remembering the first house. It is right to grieve what was lost even while rejoicing in what is new."},
{q:"What could the people not discern?", options:["The noise of the shout of joy from the noise of the weeping of the people","The sound of the trumpets from the cymbals","The singing of the priests from the Levites","The voices of the old from the young"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:13",verse:"So that the people could not discern the noise of the shout of joy from the noise of the weeping of the people: for the people shouted with a loud shout, and the noise was heard afar off.", insight:"Joy and weeping sounded as one noise. God holds our mixed feelings together in His presence."},
{q:"How far off was the noise of the people heard?", options:["Afar off","Throughout the land of Judah","Unto the cities of Samaria","To the borders of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 3:13",verse:"So that the people could not discern the noise of the shout of joy from the noise of the weeping of the people: for the people shouted with a loud shout, and the noise was heard afar off.", insight:"The sound was heard afar off. Genuine worship cannot be kept quiet."}
]},
{n:4, name:"Opposition Rises", seal:{ref:"Ezra 4:3",verse:"But Zerubbabel, and Jeshua, and the rest of the chief of the fathers of Israel, said unto them, Ye have nothing to do with us to build an house unto our God; but we ourselves together will build unto the LORD God of Israel, as king Cyrus the king of Persia hath commanded us."}, facts:["Did you know? The 'adversaries' first offered to help. Zerubbabel refused, saying they had nothing to do with building God's house, and the friendly offer turned into open opposition.","Did you know? The enemies' letter accused Jerusalem of being 'the rebellious and the bad city.' They warned Artaxerxes that a rebuilt Jerusalem would stop paying toll, tribute, and custom.","Did you know? The work stopped for years. The opposition's letter succeeded, and building ceased until the second year of Darius."], questions:[
{q:"Who heard that the children of the captivity were building the temple of the LORD?", options:["The adversaries of Judah and Benjamin","The priests of Bethel","The governors of Persia","The merchants of Tyre"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:1",verse:"Now when the adversaries of Judah and Benjamin heard that the children of the captivity builded the temple unto the LORD God of Israel;", insight:"The adversaries heard about the building. Doing God's work will always draw attention, friendly and hostile."},
{q:"What did the adversaries offer Zerubbabel?", options:["Let us build with you","Let us carry your timber","Let us guard your workers","Let us pay your tribute"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:2",verse:"Then they came to Zerubbabel, and to the chief of the fathers, and said unto them, Let us build with you: for we seek your God, as ye do; and we do sacrifice unto him since the days of Esar-haddon king of Assur, which brought us up hither.", insight:"The offer to help sounded spiritual. Not every offer of help comes from a pure heart; discernment matters."},
{q:"The adversaries claimed to seek God and sacrifice to him since whose days?", options:["Esarhaddon king of Assur","Cyrus king of Persia","Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon","Tiglathpileser king of Assyria"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:2",verse:"Then they came to Zerubbabel, and to the chief of the fathers, and said unto them, Let us build with you: for we seek your God, as ye do; and we do sacrifice unto him since the days of Esar-haddon king of Assur, which brought us up hither.", insight:"They claimed to sacrifice to God since Esarhaddon's days. Long religious talk does not prove a right heart."},
{q:"What was Zerubbabel's answer to their offer?", options:["Ye have nothing to do with us to build an house unto our God","Bring your offering to the altar first","Wait until the king gives leave","Build your own house in Samaria"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:3",verse:"But Zerubbabel, and Jeshua, and the rest of the chief of the fathers of Israel, said unto them, Ye have nothing to do with us to build an house unto our God; but we ourselves together will build unto the LORD God of Israel, as king Cyrus the king of Persia hath commanded us.", insight:"Ye have nothing to do with us was a firm no. Protecting God's work sometimes means refusing compromise."},
{q:"How did the people of the land answer being refused a share in the building?", options:["Weakened the hands of Judah and troubled them in building","Helped them willingly anyway","Left the country in anger","Sent gifts to the temple"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:4",verse:"Then the people of the land weakened the hands of the people of Judah, and troubled them in building,", insight:"Refused helpers became open hinderers. Not every offer of help is friendly; discernment protects the work."},
{q:"What did the people of the land then do?", options:["Weakened the hands of the people of Judah, and troubled them in building","Joined them with glad hearts","Sent them timber from Lebanon","Paid their tribute for them"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:4",verse:"Then the people of the land weakened the hands of the people of Judah, and troubled them in building,", insight:"Opposition weakened hands and troubled builders. Expect resistance to wear you down; keep building anyway."},
{q:"Whom did they hire against the Jews?", options:["Counsellors, to frustrate their purpose","Soldiers, to burn the timber","Scribes, to alter the decree","Priests, to stop the sacrifices"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:5",verse:"And hired counsellors against them, to frustrate their purpose, all the days of Cyrus king of Persia, even until the reign of Darius king of Persia.", insight:"Hired counsellors worked to frustrate the purpose. Some opposition is organized and paid for; pray accordingly."},
{q:"How long did the hired counsellors work against them?", options:["All the days of Cyrus, even until the reign of Darius","One year only","Seventy years","Until the death of Zerubbabel"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:5",verse:"And hired counsellors against them, to frustrate their purpose, all the days of Cyrus king of Persia, even until the reign of Darius king of Persia.", insight:"The scheming lasted from Cyrus to Darius. Spiritual opposition is patient, so believers must be persistent."},
{q:"In the reign of Ahasuerus, what was written against the inhabitants of Judah and Jerusalem?", options:["An accusation","A decree of favor","A letter of thanks","A bill of sale"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:6",verse:"And in the reign of Ahasuerus, in the beginning of his reign, wrote they unto him an accusation against the inhabitants of Judah and Jerusalem.", insight:"An accusation was written in Ahasuerus's reign. Lies on paper can travel far; truth still outlasts them."},
{q:"In the days of Artaxerxes, who wrote a letter unto the king?", options:["Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of their companions","Rehum the chancellor and Shimshai the scribe","Tatnai and Shetharboznai","Haggai and Zechariah"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:7",verse:"And in the days of Artaxerxes wrote Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of their companions, unto Artaxerxes king of Persia; and the writing of the letter was written in the Syrian tongue, and interpreted in the Syrian tongue.", insight:"Bishlam, Mithredath, and Tabeel put their names on the letter. Opponents of God's work often act openly and boldly."},
{q:"Who was Rehum?", options:["The chancellor","The scribe","The governor","The treasurer"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:8",verse:"Rehum the chancellor and Shimshai the scribe wrote a letter against Jerusalem to Artaxerxes the king in this sort:", insight:"Rehum the chancellor used his office against God's people. Power in wrong hands becomes a weapon against the church."},
{q:"Who was Shimshai?", options:["The scribe","The chancellor","The governor","The priest"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:8",verse:"Rehum the chancellor and Shimshai the scribe wrote a letter against Jerusalem to Artaxerxes the king in this sort:", insight:"Shimshai the scribe wrote the lies down. Words are powerful tools, for truth or for harm."},
{q:"The letter listed many peoples settled in Samaria by whom?", options:["The great and noble Asnappar","Esarhaddon king of Assur","Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon","Cyrus king of Persia"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:10",verse:"And the rest of the nations whom the great and noble Asnapper brought over, and set in the cities of Samaria, and the rest that are on this side the river, and at such a time.", insight:"The letter listed many settled peoples. Opposition often gathers a crowd; numbers do not make a cause right."},
{q:"What did the writers call Jerusalem in their letter?", options:["The rebellious and the bad city","The holy city of peace","The city of the great king","The city of refuge"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:12",verse:"Be it known unto the king, that the Jews which came up from thee to us are come unto Jerusalem, building the rebellious and the bad city, and have set up the walls thereof, and joined the foundations.", insight:"They called Jerusalem the rebellious and the bad city. The world often mislabels God's people; God knows the truth."},
{q:"What did they warn the king the Jews would stop paying if the city were built?", options:["Toll, tribute, and custom","The temple tax","The firstfruits","The freewill offering"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:13",verse:"Be it known now unto the king, that, if this city be builded, and the walls set up again, then will they not pay toll, tribute, and custom, and so thou shalt endamage the revenue of the kings.", insight:"The money argument, toll and tribute, was their leverage. Worldly interests often dress up as loyalty to the king."},
{q:"What did the letter writers say to show their loyalty to the king?", options:["They had maintenance from the king's palace","They were born in Persia","They had served in his army","They loved the city of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:14",verse:"Now because we have maintenance from the king’s palace, and it was not meet for us to see the king’s dishonour, therefore have we sent and certified the king;", insight:"We have maintenance from the king's palace was their claim of loyalty. Serving power for profit is not the same as serving God."},
{q:"What did they urge the king to search?", options:["The book of the records of thy fathers","The vessels of the temple","The gates of the city","The houses of the priests"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:15",verse:"That search may be made in the book of the records of thy fathers: so shalt thou find in the book of the records, and know that this city is a rebellious city, and hurtful unto kings and provinces, and that they have moved sedition within the same of old time: for which cause was this city destroyed.", insight:"They urged a search of the records. God's enemies sometimes demand the very evidence that will vindicate His people."},
{q:"After his search, what did Artaxerxes command?", options:["Give ye now commandment to cause these men to cease","Let the work go forward","Send the vessels back","Double the tribute"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:21",verse:"Give ye now commandment to cause these men to cease, and that this city be not builded, until another commandment shall be given from me.", insight:"The king ordered the men to cease. Human decrees can pause God's work, but they cannot cancel His purpose."},
{q:"How did Rehum and his companions enforce the order?", options:["Went up in haste to Jerusalem, and made them to cease by force and power","Sealed the temple doors with the king's ring","Arrested Zerubbabel and Jeshua","Burned the timber at Joppa"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:23",verse:"Now when the copy of king Artaxerxes’ letter was read before Rehum, and Shimshai the scribe, and their companions, they went up in haste to Jerusalem unto the Jews, and made them to cease by force and power.", insight:"They stopped the work by force and power. Force can halt building for a season, but it cannot kill God's plan."},
{q:"Until when did the work of the house of God cease?", options:["The second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia","The seventh year of Artaxerxes","The death of Cyrus","The coming of Ezra"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 4:24",verse:"Then ceased the work of the house of God which is at Jerusalem. So it ceased unto the second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia.", insight:"The work ceased until Darius's second year. God's delays are not God's denials; the pause had an end date."}
]}
,
{n:5, name:"The Work Resumes", seal:{ref:"Ezra 5:5",verse:"But the eye of their God was upon the elders of the Jews, that they could not cause them to cease, till the matter came to Darius: and then they returned answer by letter concerning this matter."}, facts:["Did you know? Two prophets restarted the work. Haggai and Zechariah preached, and Zerubbabel and Jeshua picked up their tools again.","Did you know? Tatnai never got the stop order he expected. The eye of their God was upon the elders, so the Jews kept building while his letter traveled to Darius.","Did you know? The Jews' defense rested on an old decree. They asked Darius to search the royal archives for Cyrus's order, and the search would settle everything."], questions:[
{q:"Which two prophets prophesied unto the Jews in Judah and Jerusalem?", options:["Haggai the prophet, and Zechariah the son of Iddo","Ezra the scribe and Nehemiah","Hosea and Amos","Isaiah and Jeremiah"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:1",verse:"Then the prophets, Haggai the prophet, and Zechariah the son of Iddo, prophesied unto the Jews that were in Judah and Jerusalem in the name of the God of Israel, even unto them.", insight:"Haggai and Zechariah prophesied, and the work restarted. God's Word through His messengers rekindles stalled obedience."},
{q:"In whose name did they prophesy?", options:["The name of the God of Israel","The name of Cyrus","The name of Darius","The name of the king of Persia"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:1",verse:"Then the prophets, Haggai the prophet, and Zechariah the son of Iddo, prophesied unto the Jews that were in Judah and Jerusalem in the name of the God of Israel, even unto them.", insight:"They prophesied in the name of the God of Israel. True preaching carries God's authority, not man's ideas."},
{q:"Who rose up and began to build the house of God which is at Jerusalem?", options:["Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak","Ezra and the Levites","Nehemiah and the nobles","Sheshbazzar and the elders"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:2",verse:"Then rose up Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and began to build the house of God which is at Jerusalem: and with them were the prophets of God helping them.", insight:"Zerubbabel and Jeshua rose up and began to build. Hearing God's word should move us to action."},
{q:"Who was with them, helping them?", options:["The prophets of God","The army of Persia","The counsellors of the king","The merchants of Tyre"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:2",verse:"Then rose up Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and began to build the house of God which is at Jerusalem: and with them were the prophets of God helping them.", insight:"The prophets were with them, helping. Preachers should stand beside the workers, not just speak to them."},
{q:"Who came to them as governor on this side the river?", options:["Tatnai","Shetharboznai","Rehum","Shimshai"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:3",verse:"At the same time came to them Tatnai, governor on this side the river, and Shethar-boznai, and their companions, and said thus unto them, Who hath commanded you to build this house, and to make up this wall?", insight:"Tatnai the governor came asking questions. Legitimate authority may question us; we can answer with truth."},
{q:"What question did Tatnai and his companions ask?", options:["Who hath commanded you to build this house, and to make up this wall?","Where is the decree of Cyrus?","Who are the priests among you?","When will the work be finished?"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:3",verse:"At the same time came to them Tatnai, governor on this side the river, and Shethar-boznai, and their companions, and said thus unto them, Who hath commanded you to build this house, and to make up this wall?", insight:"Who commanded you to build was a fair question with a strong answer: God did, through Cyrus."},
{q:"In the letter, how did Tatnai report their demand for the builders' names?", options:["What are the names of the men that make this building?","Tell us the number of your workmen","Show us your genealogy","Name the prophets among you"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:4",verse:"Then said we unto them after this manner, What are the names of the men that make this building?", insight:"They were asked the names of the builders. Standing for God may put your name on someone's list; stand anyway."},
{q:"Why could the adversaries not make the Jews cease?", options:["The eye of their God was upon the elders of the Jews","The Jews had armed themselves","The king's guard protected them","The river had flooded"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:5",verse:"But the eye of their God was upon the elders of the Jews, that they could not cause them to cease, till the matter came to Darius: and then they returned answer by letter concerning this matter.", insight:"The eye of God was upon the elders. God's watchful care is the best protection His people have."},
{q:"What did Tatnai ask the builders when he questioned them?", options:["What are the names of the men that make this building?","Who gave you this gold?","When will you finish?","Where is your king?"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:4",verse:"Then said we unto them after this manner, What are the names of the men that make this building?", insight:"He asked for names, but God already knew them. Men investigate; God watches over."},
{q:"To whom did Tatnai send the copy of his letter?", options:["Darius the king","Cyrus the king","Artaxerxes the king","Ahasuerus the king"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:6",verse:"The copy of the letter that Tatnai, governor on this side the river, and Shethar-boznai, and his companions the Apharsachites, which were on this side the river, sent unto Darius the king:", insight:"Tatnai wrote to Darius, not acting rashly. Even opponents can be fair when God restrains them."},
{q:"How did the Jews describe themselves in their answer to Tatnai?", options:["Servants of the God of heaven and earth","Sons of the king of Persia","Builders of the king's palace","Keepers of the king's treasure"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:11",verse:"And thus they returned us answer, saying, We are the servants of the God of heaven and earth, and build the house that was builded these many years ago, which a great king of Israel builded and set up.", insight:"Servants of the God of heaven and earth was their identity. Knowing whose you are steadies you under questioning."},
{q:"Who did they say had built and set up the house many years before?", options:["A great king of Israel","A mighty king of Babylon","A prince of Persia","A judge of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:11",verse:"And thus they returned us answer, saying, We are the servants of the God of heaven and earth, and build the house that was builded these many years ago, which a great king of Israel builded and set up.", insight:"A great king of Israel had built the house long before. They stood in a long line of faith; we do too."},
{q:"Why did God give their fathers into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar?", options:["Because they provoked the God of heaven unto wrath","Because they refused to pay tribute","Because they built the high places","Because they fled to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:12",verse:"But after that our fathers had provoked the God of heaven unto wrath, he gave them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, the Chaldean, who destroyed this house, and carried the people away into Babylon.", insight:"Their fathers provoked God and lost the temple. Honest confession of past sin is part of a true defense."},
{q:"What did Nebuchadnezzar do to the house?", options:["Destroyed this house, and carried the people away to Babylon","Burned the vessels of gold","Slew the priests at the altar","Broke down the walls of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:12",verse:"But after that our fathers had provoked the God of heaven unto wrath, he gave them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, the Chaldean, who destroyed this house, and carried the people away into Babylon.", insight:"Nebuchadnezzar destroyed the house and carried the people away. Sin has real consequences, but God still restores."},
{q:"In whose first year was the decree made to build the house of God?", options:["Cyrus","Darius","Artaxerxes","Ahasuerus"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:13",verse:"But in the first year of Cyrus the king of Babylon the same king Cyrus made a decree to build this house of God.", insight:"Cyrus's first year decree was their legal ground. God's people can appeal to every lawful means He provides."},
{q:"What did Cyrus do with the gold and silver vessels Nebuchadnezzar had taken?", options:["Delivered them unto Sheshbazzar","Melted them for tribute","Placed them in his own palace","Sent them to the governors"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:14",verse:"And the vessels also of gold and silver of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took out of the temple that was in Jerusalem, and brought them into the temple of Babylon, those did Cyrus the king take out of the temple of Babylon, and they were delivered unto one, whose name was Sheshbazzar, whom he had made governor;", insight:"Cyrus returned the stolen vessels. What God intends for His house, He brings back in His time."},
{q:"Whom had Cyrus made governor, to whom the vessels were delivered?", options:["Sheshbazzar","Zerubbabel","Tatnai","Jeshua"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:14",verse:"And the vessels also of gold and silver of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took out of the temple that was in Jerusalem, and brought them into the temple of Babylon, those did Cyrus the king take out of the temple of Babylon, and they were delivered unto one, whose name was Sheshbazzar, whom he had made governor;", insight:"Sheshbazzar, made governor, received the vessels. God positions the right people to carry holy things."},
{q:"What did Cyrus command Sheshbazzar to do with the vessels?", options:["Carry them to the temple in Jerusalem, and let the house of God be builded in his place","Bring them to the king's treasury","Divide them among the priests","Hide them until Darius reigns"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:15",verse:"And said unto him, Take these vessels, go, carry them into the temple that is in Jerusalem, and let the house of God be builded in his place.", insight:"Let the house of God be builded in his place. God's house belongs in its God appointed place, nowhere else."},
{q:"Who came and laid the foundation of the house of God which is in Jerusalem?", options:["Sheshbazzar","Zerubbabel","Jeshua","Haggai"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:16",verse:"Then came the same Sheshbazzar, and laid the foundation of the house of God which is in Jerusalem: and since that time even until now hath it been in building, and yet it is not finished.", insight:"Sheshbazzar laid the foundation long before. Faithful beginnings matter, even when finishing takes years."},
{q:"What did Tatnai ask Darius to have searched for?", options:["Whether a decree was made of Cyrus to build the house of God at Jerusalem","The names of all the builders","The number of the vessels","The book of the records of the fathers"], a:0, ref:"Ezra 5:17",verse:"Now therefore, if it seem good to the king, let there be search made in the king’s treasure house, which is there at Babylon, whether it be so, that a decree was made of Cyrus the king to build this house of God at Jerusalem, and let the king send his pleasure to us concerning this matter.", insight:"Tatnai asked for a search of the archives. God's cause can survive scrutiny; truth welcomes investigation."}
]}
]);
